 "On 19-22 June 1941 a Soviet team led by Mikhail Gerasimov opened the tomb of the conqueror Timur (Tamerlane) in the Gur-e-Amir mausoleum, Samarkand. Legend held that disturbing it would unleash war, and an inscription was reported to warn against it. Germany invaded the USSR on 22 June 1941. The remains were reburied with Islamic rites in November 1942, shortly before the Soviet victory at Stalingrad. The examination confirmed that Timur was tall and lame in the right leg, matching historical accounts.",
